              <p class="text-left">
                  <br>The Chemical Augmented Reality Project has been established to enrich the academic journey of Dalhousie students. 
                  Our mission is to provide an unparalleled immersive experience by harnessing the power of Augmented Reality (AR) to visualize intricate 3D molecular models.
                  At the heart of the web application lies the AR.js library, a development technology that detects markers, 
                  enabling a captivating list of 3D models directly accessible through your web browser. 
                  Through our passion for science and technology, we bring to life dynamic molecular models, generated from .mol files. 
                  The classic "ball and stick" representation is emulated, displaying both accuracy and familiarity 
                  for users engaging with complex chemical structures.<br><br><br>
              </p>
